Spring Data JPA already marks `save()`, `delete()`, and similar write methods with `@Transactional` internally. The key is: **service-level transactions** span multiple repository calls.

```java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    @Transactional  // ONE transaction for the whole method
    public void placeOrder(Order order, List<OrderItem> items) {
        Order saved = orderRepo.save(order);      // part of transaction
        items.forEach(item -> {
            item.setOrder(saved);
            itemRepo.save(item);                  // same transaction
        });
        inventoryService.reduceStock(items);     // same transaction
        // if anything throws RuntimeException → ALL rolled back
    }
}
```

